# Cloudflare Pages — response headers for the Finance Dashboard
#
# Asset filenames are NOT content-hashed, so the iMIS iParts always point at the
# same URLs (fd-core.js, fd-styles.css, …). `no-cache` forces revalidation so a
# new deploy is picked up immediately instead of serving stale JS/CSS from the
# edge or browser cache. The files are small, so the conditional 304 round-trip
# is negligible.
#
# Do NOT add immutable caching here without content-hashing the filenames first —
# a stale script against a fresh entry HTML is the classic failure mode, and it
# surfaces as a corrupted-content / CORS error rather than as anything obvious.
#
# Access-Control-Allow-Origin is defensive: the iParts load these via
# <script src> / <link>, which need no CORS, but a wildcard keeps any future
# fetch() use working when loaded cross-origin from the iMIS domain.

/*
  Cache-Control: no-cache
  Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *
